        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b7a42161-e2fa-5569-9d66-ee7eae31b64a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Saddleback Mountain, Sandy River Plantation, Rangeley, Franklin County, Maine, Bangor, Neilston, Scotland\n- Organizations: Saddleback Maine, WRGY\n- People: William Shamus O'Brien\n- Topics: Ski resorts, mountains, radio stations, soccer\n\nFacts:\n- William Shamus O'Brien was born on November 29, 1907 in Neilston, Scotland.\n- Saddleback Mountain is a mountain in Sandy River Plantation, Franklin County, Maine, near Rangeley.\n- Saddleback Mountain is one of Maine's highest mountains and one of fourteen in the state with more than 2,000 feet of topographic prominence.\n- Saddleback Maine is a ski resort on the northwestern slopes of Saddleback Mountain in Sandy River Plantation, near Rangeley, Maine.\n- Saddleback Mountain is the site of the Saddleback Maine ski resort.\n- Saddleback Maine is the third largest ski area in Maine by trails, lifts, snowmaking percentage, vertical drop, and skier days, with 66 trails, 5 lifts, 85% snowmaking, and a 2,000-foot vertical drop.\n- WRGY has studios on Main Street in Rangeley and its transmitter is atop Saddleback Mountain.\n- William Shamus O'Brien died on November 28, 1981 in Bangor, Maine.\n- William Shamus O'Brien was a U.S.-Scottish soccer inside left.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
